language ESSENCE'  1.0
$ Vessel loading: place every container on the deck, without overlap and keeping the required separation between containers of the given classes. A container may be rotated by 90 degrees.
given n_containers : int(1..)
given deck_width, deck_length : int(1..)
given width, length : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_containers)] of int(1..)
given classes : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_containers)] of int(1..)
given separation_dim1, separation_dim2 : int(1..)
given separation : matrix indexed by [int(1..separation_dim1), int(1..separation_dim2)] of int(0..)
find left, right : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_containers)] of int(0..deck_width)
find top, bottom : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_containers)] of int(0..deck_length)
$ whether each container is turned by 90 degrees
find rotated : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_containers)] of bool
$ extent of each container along the deck width and along the deck length
find extent_w, extent_l : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_containers)] of int(1..max(deck_width, deck_length))
branching on [rotated, left, top]
such that
$ the container's extent along the width is its width, or its length when turned
forAll i : int(1..n_containers) . extent_w[i] = width[i] + toInt(rotated[i]) * (length[i] - width[i]),
$ the container's extent along the length is the other side
forAll i : int(1..n_containers) . extent_l[i] = width[i] + length[i] - extent_w[i],
$ each container occupies its extent from its left and top edges, and stays on the deck
forAll i : int(1..n_containers) . right[i] = left[i] + extent_w[i],
forAll i : int(1..n_containers) . bottom[i] = top[i] + extent_l[i],
forAll i : int(1..n_containers) . right[i] <= deck_width,
forAll i : int(1..n_containers) . bottom[i] <= deck_length,
$ no two containers overlap, and containers of classes with a required separation are at least that far apart along the deck or across the deck
forAll i : int(1..n_containers) . forAll j : int(i+1..n_containers) . ((right[i] + separation[classes[i], classes[j]] <= left[j]) \/ (right[j] + separation[classes[i], classes[j]] <= left[i]) \/ (bottom[i] + separation[classes[i], classes[j]] <= top[j]) \/ (bottom[j] + separation[classes[i], classes[j]] <= top[i]))
